From 564271aa55e96a8c63a45b825e4c3b45bdce0200 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Stimola <francesco-stimola@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:40:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] nouveau: give the vc1 vp the picture height

The VC-1 VP parameters take the macroblock-aligned height, while NVIDIA's
driver passes the picture height there, 1080 for a 1920x1080 stream. When
the height is not a multiple of 16, motion vectors pointing below the
picture then read the decoded rows of the last macroblock row instead of
the repeated bottom edge, and the error spreads through the following
frames.

Pass the picture height.

Tested on a GeForce GT 240M (VP4): FFmpeg's sample vc1-wmapro.ism,
240x104, now matches software decoding; before, 118 of its 120 frames
differed, starting from the bottom edge. With 0015, the 1920x1080
interlaced stream ilaced_twomv matches too.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_vp3_video_vp.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_vp3_video_vp.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_vp3_video_vp.c
index 63264a7..fc70b4f 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_vp3_video_vp.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_vp3_video_vp.c
@@ -377,7 +377,7 @@ nouveau_vp3_fill_picparm_vc1_vp(struct nouveau_vp3_decoder *dec,
    vc->ofs[5] = vc->ofs[3];
    vc->ofs[0] = vc->ofs[2] = 0;
    vc->width = dec->base.width;
-   vc->height = mb(dec->base.height)<<4;
+   vc->height = dec->base.height;
    vc->unk0c = vc->unk10 = mb(dec->base.width)<<4; // Stride
    vc->pad = vc->pad2 = 0;
    nouveau_vp3_inter_sizes(dec, 1, &ring, &vc->bucket_size, &vc->inter_ring_data_size);
